// Five equal bars on 3:5, lightened outside a heart (radius 0.986, default spread, at fly 2.5 hoist 0.99).
// The outline is the same heart shrunk by half its 0.045 width (radius 0.9635, spread 1.3944), so its outer edge is the heart's.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Ceteroromantic flag"
  designer "Pride-Flags (DeviantArt)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  source "https://www.deviantart.com/pride-flags/art/Ceteroromantic-2-607943801"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20181217215130/https://pride-color-schemes.tumblr.com/tagged/ceteroromantic"
  note "Designer's own publication: 'Ceteroromantic (2)' by Pride-Flags on DeviantArt, published 9 May 2016 at 21:35 Pacific time (10 May UTC). Its page defines cetero- (formerly skolio-) as attraction to non-binary people, and says 'Cetero- design by me, based on the original by' SavvyRed, linking SavvyRed's DeviantArt and a post on the Tumblr blog savvysweet (118695661933, 'skoliosexual'), which wasn't read. The Tumblr blog pride-color-schemes, run by the same people, shows the five-stripe ceterosexual flag on 1 July 2016 as yellow, green, pink, white and black, 'Designed by: Me', with a 'Ceteroromantic only version with a transparent heart with pink outline', which is this flag. Neither post gives meanings for the pink stripe; SavvyRed's 2013 flag gives the other four colors' meanings."
  note "Everything here is read from the designer's own 5000 by 3000 pixel image: the 3:5 proportion, five equal bars of 600 pixels, and the colors. Inside the heart the bars are #fffc01, #218d03, #f556e9, #ffffff and #000000; the yellow, green, white and black are exactly those of SavvyRed's 2013 image. Outside the heart they are lighter: #fffe80, #90c681, #faabf4, #ffffff and #808080. The outline is #f656ea, one unit from the pink stripe, and 45 pixels wide, inside the heart's edge."
  note "The heart is the format's heart shape, an approximation of the image's drawing, which has slightly curved sides and a deeper notch. It is the same size and place as the hearts of the other heart flags Pride-Flags uploaded that night, whose radius, 0.986 of a hoist of 3, and center, 0.99 below the top, were fitted to those images: centered across the flag, the lobes touching the top edge and the tip the bottom edge."
}
palette {
  yellow "#fffc01"
  green "#218d03"
  pink "#f556e9"
  white "#ffffff"
  black "#000000"
  pale-yellow "#fffe80"
  pale-green "#90c681"
  pale-pink "#faabf4"
  grey "#808080"
  outline-pink "#f656ea"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars pale-yellow pale-green pale-pink white grey

bars yellow green pink white black {
  clip {
    heart {
      radius 0.986
      at fly=2.5 hoist=0.99
    }
  }
}

charge heart outline-pink {
  radius 0.9635
  spread 1.3944
  at fly=2.5 hoist=0.99
  hollow 0.045
}
